Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add CI check that catches broken iOS project files before
 merge (Task #467)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem
- Task #466 introduced a deterministic pbxproj generator
  (ios-native/scripts/generate-pbxproj.mjs), but nothing prevented
  someone from hand-editing project.pbxproj or forgetting to re-run the
  generator after adding a new Swift file.

Changes
- ios-native/scripts/generate-pbxproj.mjs: refactored to export GROUPS,
  PACKAGES, SOURCE_ROOT, PBXPROJ_PATH, build, and lint. The disk-write
  side effect is now gated on `import.meta.url === argv[1]`, so other
  tools can import the module without overwriting the committed
  project.pbxproj.
- ios-native/scripts/check-pbxproj.mjs (new): walks
  ios-native/CommandComms/ for *.swift files and fails if any are not
  declared in GROUPS, then regenerates the pbxproj in memory and fails
  if it differs from the committed copy. Prints actionable fix
  instructions and exits non-zero on failure.
- .github/workflows/ios-pbxproj-check.yml (new): runs the check on
  every push and pull_request using Node 20.
- ios-native/README.md: new "CI guard" subsection under "Regenerating
  the Xcode project" describing the check and how to fix a failure
  locally.

Verification
- node ios-native/scripts/check-pbxproj.mjs → OK on a clean tree.
- Adding a stray Audio/Bogus.swift → fails with the missing-inventory
  message and exit 1.
- Hand-appending bytes to project.pbxproj → fails with the
  out-of-date message and exit 1; re-running the generator restores
  green.

Follow-up proposed
- #468: cross-check PACKAGES against Package.resolved so SPM version
  drift is also caught at CI time.

